"use strict";
window.LC_CHUNKS=window.LC_CHUNKS||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["school_mathematics_en"]=window.LC_CHUNKS["school_mathematics_en"]||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["school_mathematics_en"][5]={"school_mathematics_en:M5-L1":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L1\">M5-L1 – Sequences, recursion and mathematical induction<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M5 – Sequences and series<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Upper secondary education · elective\nextension<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prior knowledge:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L17&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M1-L17<\/a>; <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L19&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M1-L19<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Context:<\/strong> Elective extension informed by Bavaria’s\nLehrplanPLUS M12; not a nationwide requirement.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Learning objectives<\/h2>\n<p>Describe sequences explicitly and recursively, construct proofs by\nmathematical induction, and investigate monotonicity, bounds and limits.\nDistinguish a conjecture based on a few terms from a statement about all\nnatural numbers.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sequences as functions<\/h2>\n<p>A real sequence assigns exactly one real number to every natural\nnumber from a starting index onward. Here we start at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nOrder matters: a sequence is not an unordered set. An explicit formula\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ndirectly from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\na recurrence uses earlier terms and an initial value. For example,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_n=3n+2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nproduces\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>5<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>11<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>14<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>…<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">5,8,11,14,\\ldots<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nequivalently,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_1=5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{n+1}=a_n+3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAn arithmetic sequence has constant difference\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_n=a_1+(n-1)d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nA geometric sequence satisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{n+1}=qa_n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><msup><mi>q<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_n=a_1q^{n-1}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe latter formula applies for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nwith a separately specified initial term. Do not confuse the first term\nwith the starting index.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Recursion and induction<\/h2>\n<p>Consider\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_1=2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{n+1}=(a_n+6)/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe first values are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>5.5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2,4,5,5.5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nA possible explicit formula is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_n=6-4\\cdot2^{-(n-1)}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nTo prove it, first establish the base case: for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthe formula gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>6<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">6-4=2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIn the induction step assume the claim for an arbitrary\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k\\ge1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThen<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><mo>+<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><mn>2<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{k+1}=\\frac{6-4\\cdot2^{-(k-1)}+6}{2}=6-4\\cdot2^{-k}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>This is precisely the claim for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k+1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nTogether the two steps prove the formula for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe assumption for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nalone is not a proof; deriving the next case is essential.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Monotonicity and boundedness<\/h2>\n<p>A sequence is nondecreasing if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>≥<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{n+1}\\ge a_n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand nonincreasing if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>≤<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{n+1}\\le a_n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor all indices under consideration. Strict monotonicity uses strict\ninequalities. An upper bound\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nsatisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>B<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_n\\le B<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\na lower bound\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>b<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nsatisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\le a_n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor our recursive sequence,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{n+1}-a_n=2\\cdot2^{-(n-1)}&gt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAlso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\le a_n&lt;6<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nA plot shows only finitely many points; the proof follows from the\nformula. The sequence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-1)^n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis bounded but not monotone and has no limit.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-school-mathematics-en/media/img/S_MAT_037_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Discrete sequence terms from n equal to 1 through 10 between 2 and 6; dashed upper bound at 6.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: The recursive sequence approaches the upper bound 6\nfrom below.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Limits<\/h2>\n<p>A limit\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmeans that for every positive error tolerance\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ε<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varepsilon<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthere is an index\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nsuch that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mi>L<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>ε<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|a_n-L|&lt;\\varepsilon<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mi>N<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge N<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIndividual terms need not reach\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe monotone convergence theorem states that a nondecreasing real\nsequence bounded above converges; likewise a nonincreasing sequence\nbounded below converges. For our sequence we have\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|a_n-6|=4\\cdot2^{-(n-1)}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThis error halves at every step and tends to zero. For a tolerance of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>0.1<\/mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N=7<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nsuffices because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>64<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.0625<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>0.1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4/64=0.0625&lt;0.1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAll subsequent errors are smaller.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>From model to proof<\/h2>\n<p>In a simplified temperature model, half the difference from the\nambient temperature of 20 °C is removed each minute. With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>12<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_1=12<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nwe have\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mn>20<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_{n+1}=(T_n+20)/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe difference\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>20<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">20-T_n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nhalves, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>20<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_n=20-8\\cdot2^{-(n-1)}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe sequence increases and approaches 20 °C. The equation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>L<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>20<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=(L+20)/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ngives a possible limit but already assumes convergence. In contrast,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_1=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><msub><mi>b<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_{n+1}=-b_n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ngives the possible limit equation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mi>L<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=-L<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nyet does not converge. The temperature model assumes constant\nsurroundings and a constant adjustment rate; real measurements may\ndiffer.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S7\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-check<\/h2>\n<h3 id=\"exercises\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Give the explicit formula and sixth term for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_1=7<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{n+1}=a_n-2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Prove by induction that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mi>⋯<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>n<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1+3+\\cdots+(2n-1)=n^2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Investigate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_n=3+1/n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor monotonicity, bounds and limit.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">For the sequence in S3, find the smallest index from which\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>100<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|a_n-6|&lt;1/100<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nholds.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Investigate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><mi>/<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c_n=(-1)^n/n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor monotonicity and convergence.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<details class=\"lc-solutions\" data-lc-section=\"S7\"><summary>Show solutions<\/summary>\n<div>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_n=7-2(n-1)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mn>6<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_6=-3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Base:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mn>1<\/mn><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1=1^2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nHypothesis: the sum through term\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>k<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k^2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nStep:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>+<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>k<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k^2+(2(k+1)-1)=k^2+2k+1=(k+1)^2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe claim holds for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b<\/mi><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>b<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_{n+1}-b_n=-1/[n(n+1)]&lt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWe have\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><msub><mi>b<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3&lt;b_n\\le4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><mo>→<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/n\\to0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>→<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_n\\to3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">At\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=9<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>256<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>64<\/mn><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>100<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4/256=1/64&gt;1/100<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=10<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>512<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>128<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>100<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4/512=1/128&lt;1/100<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nSince the error halves,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N=10<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis minimal.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Not monotone: alternating signs with decreasing magnitude;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><msub><mi>c<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><mo>→<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|c_n|=1/n\\to0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>→<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c_n\\to0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/div>\n<\/details>\n<h2 id=\"S8\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://openstax.org/books/calculus-volume-2/pages/5-1-sequences\">OpenStax\n– Calculus Volume 2, 5.1 Sequences<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Sequences, monotonicity and\nconvergence · Last accessed: 2026-11-24 · Content verified:\n2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://discrete.openmathbooks.org/dmoi4/sec_seq-induction.html\">Oscar\nLevin – Discrete Mathematics: An Open Introduction, Proof by\nInduction<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Induction principle and proof structure · Last accessed:\n2026-11-24 · Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","school_mathematics_en:M5-L2":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L2\">M5-L2 – Series and Taylor polynomials<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M5 – Sequences and series<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Upper secondary education · elective\nextension<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prior knowledge:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M5&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M5-L1<\/a>; <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M2&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M2-L4<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Context:<\/strong> Elective extension informed by Bavaria’s\nLehrplanPLUS M12; not a nationwide requirement.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Learning objectives<\/h2>\n<p>Calculate partial sums of geometric series, justify convergence or\ndivergence, and approximate the exponential function by Taylor\npolynomials with an error bound.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sequence, partial sum and series<\/h2>\n<p>A sequence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(a_n)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ndetermines the partial-sum sequence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msubsup><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><mi>N<\/mi><\/msubsup><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_N=\\sum_{n=1}^N a_n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAn infinite series\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><mi>∞<\/mi><\/msubsup><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty a_n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nconverges exactly when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>S<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_N<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nhas a finite limit. Only then do we call that limit the sum of the\nseries. For example,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_n=2^{-n}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nbegins\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2,1/4,1/8<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nthe partial sums are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2,3/4,7/8<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe sequence and the series have different limits. Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>S<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>S<\/mi><mrow><mi>N<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_N=S_N-S_{N-1}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe terms of any convergent series must tend to zero. The converse is\nfalse.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Geometric series<\/h2>\n<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N\\ge1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q\\ne1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nset\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><msubsup><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><mrow><mi>N<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msubsup><msup><mi>q<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G_N=a\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}q^k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nSubtracting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q<\/mi><msub><mi>G<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">qG_N<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfrom\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>G<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G_N<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nleaves only the initial and final terms:<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><msub><mi>G<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><msup><mi>q<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msub><mi>G<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><msup><mi>q<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G_N-qG_N=a(1-q^N),\\qquad G_N=\\frac{a(1-q^N)}{1-q}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>N<\/mi><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G_N=Na<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|q|&lt;1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>q<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q^N<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ntends to zero and the infinite series has value\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a/(1-q)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|q|\\ge1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe terms cannot tend to zero, so the series diverges. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nevery partial sum is zero. For example,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mi>⋯<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4+2+1+\\cdots=8<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAfter five terms the partial sum is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>31<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">31/4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nthe remaining tail is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIn general, when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|q|&lt;1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe tail equals\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><msup><mi>q<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msup><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">aq^N/(1-q)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>The harmonic series<\/h2>\n<p>The terms\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ntend to zero but their series diverges. Consider the partial sums\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msubsup><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><mi>N<\/mi><\/msubsup><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_N=\\sum_{n=1}^N1/n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAfter the initial term, group the summands into blocks ending at indices\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>16<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>…<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2,4,8,16,\\ldots<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe block from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mrow><mi>j<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^{j-1}+1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mi>j<\/mi><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^j<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncontains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mrow><mi>j<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^{j-1}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nterms, each at least\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mi>j<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2^j<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nEach block therefore contributes at least\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nHence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H<\/mi><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mi>m<\/mi><\/msup><\/msub><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_{2^m}\\ge1+m/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\ge1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe partial sums are unbounded, so there is no finite limit. Even very\nslow unbounded growth is divergence.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Taylor polynomials<\/h2>\n<p>At the expansion point\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\na Taylor polynomial matches a sufficiently differentiable function in\nits value and derivatives through order\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>:<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mi>m<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><munderover><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><mi>m<\/mi><\/munderover><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>f<\/mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mi>!<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><\/msup><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_m(x)=\\sum_{k=0}^m\\frac{f^{(k)}(a)}{k!}(x-a)^k.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>Here\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f<\/mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mi>f<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^{(0)}=f<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><mi>!<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0!=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=e^x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nevery derivative has value 1 there. Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_2(x)=1+x+x^2/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>+<\/mo><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msup><mi>/<\/mi><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_3(x)=P_2(x)+x^3/6<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAt\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=0.5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>79<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>48<\/mn><mo>≈<\/mo><mn>1.645833<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_3=79/48\\approx1.645833<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nwhile\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mn>0.5<\/mn><\/msup><mo>≈<\/mo><mn>1.648721<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^{0.5}\\approx1.648721<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe approximation is local; farther from the expansion point the error\nmay be larger.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-school-mathematics-en/media/img/S_MAT_038_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Left: geometric partial sums with limit 1 and growing harmonic partial sums; right: exponential function and Taylor polynomials of degrees two and three.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Geometric and harmonic partial sums and Taylor\napproximations of exp about zero.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Error bound and Taylor series<\/h2>\n<p>As an advanced result, use Taylor’s theorem with the Lagrange\nremainder: if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis sufficiently smooth on the interval between\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><msup><mi>f<\/mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>M<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f^{(m+1)}(t)|\\le M<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthere, then<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>f<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mi>m<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>≤<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>!<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f(x)-P_m(x)|\\le\\frac{M|x-a|^{m+1}}{(m+1)!}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>For the exponential function on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>0.5<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,0.5]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nwe have\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mn>0.5<\/mn><\/msup><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M=e^{0.5}&lt;2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAt\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=0.5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe error is less than\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/msup><mi>/<\/mi><mn>24<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>192<\/mn><mo>≈<\/mo><mn>0.00521<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2(1/2)^4/24=1/192\\approx0.00521<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor any fixed real\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nchoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M=e^{|x|}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe expression\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>!<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x|^{m+1}/(m+1)!<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ntends to zero: for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthe ratio of consecutive terms is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x|/(m+2)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\neventually at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nand for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthe terms are zero. This justifies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><msubsup><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><mi>∞<\/mi><\/msubsup><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msup><mi>/<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><mi>!<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^x=\\sum_{k=0}^\\infty x^k/k!<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor this function. For other functions convergence to the function must\nbe checked separately; the existence of all derivatives alone is\ninsufficient.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S7\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-check<\/h2>\n<h3 id=\"exercises\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Calculate the sum of the first four terms and the infinite sum of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3<\/mn><msubsup><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><mi>∞<\/mi><\/msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3\\sum_{k=0}^\\infty(1/3)^k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Does\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><mi>∞<\/mi><\/msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum_{k=0}^\\infty(-1)^k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nconverge? Justify using partial sums.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Prove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H<\/mi><mn>32<\/mn><\/msub><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_{32}\\ge7/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwithout decimal arithmetic.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Calculate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_2(-1/2)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nabout zero and give an error bound with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=1/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nfind the smallest degree\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\ge0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor which the bound\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>!<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2(1/2)^{m+1}/(m+1)!<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis less than\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>0.001<\/mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.001<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<details class=\"lc-solutions\" data-lc-section=\"S7\"><summary>Show solutions<\/summary>\n<div>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>81<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>40<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G_4=(9/2)(1-1/81)=40/9<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\ninfinite sum\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>9<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">9/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">No. The partial sums alternate between 1 and 0, so have no\nlimit.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>32<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mn>5<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">32=2^5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFive blocks each contribute at least\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin addition to the initial term 1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H<\/mi><mn>32<\/mn><\/msub><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_{32}\\ge1+5/2=7/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>8<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_2(-1/2)=1-1/2+1/8=5/8<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nOn\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[-1/2,0]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/msup><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^t\\le1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>≤<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/msup><mi>/<\/mi><mn>6<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>48<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|R_2|\\le(1/2)^3/6=1/48<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">At\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthe bound is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>192<\/mn><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>0.001<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/192&gt;0.001<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nit is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>1920<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>0.001<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/1920&lt;0.001<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe bound decreases with degree, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis minimal.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/div>\n<\/details>\n<h2 id=\"S8\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://openstax.org/books/calculus-volume-2/pages/5-2-infinite-series\">OpenStax\n– Calculus Volume 2, 5.2 Infinite Series<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Geometric and harmonic\nseries · Last accessed: 2026-11-24 · Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://openstax.org/books/calculus-volume-2/pages/6-3-taylor-and-maclaurin-series\">OpenStax\n– Calculus Volume 2, 6.3 Taylor and Maclaurin Series<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Taylor\npolynomials and remainder · Last accessed: 2026-11-24 · Content\nverified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>"};
